  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Syntax of consequence",
     "texto": [
      "**Sodass** introduces a consecutive clause that explains the inevitable result of a previous action. As a subordinating conjunction, it moves the conjugated verb to the end of the sentence: **Der Sturm beschädigte die Fahrleitung, sodass kein Zug mehr abfahren konnte.**",
      "When the intensity of an adjective or adverb is emphasised, it can be separated as **so + adjective/adverb …, dass**: **Der Schaden war so groß, dass die Strecke gesperrt blieb.**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Structure",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Syntactic function",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Illustrative example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "sodass + verb at the end",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Immediate general consequence",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Wir informierten den Kunden rechtzeitig, sodass kein Konflikt entstand.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "so + Adjektiv …, dass",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Consequence weighted with intensity",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Die Verspätung war so beträchtlich, dass der Termin verschoben wurde.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ]
     ],
